BF.CONTRACT = {"title":"STATEMENT OF TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT","intro":"This statement of main terms, together with the Employee Handbook, sets out the particulars of the main terms and conditions on which Rabbit’s Foot Restaurants Ltd (the Company) of 47/48 Piccadilly, London, W1J 0DT employs: {{name}}","clauses":[{"h":"POSITION","items":[{"t":"You are employed as {{job}}. Your duties may be modified from time to time to suit the needs of the business.","sub":[]},{"t":"It is an express condition of your employment that you are prepared, whenever necessary, to transfer to alternative departments or duties within the business. This may include covering some duties normally performed by colleagues, for example during holiday periods. This flexibility is essential because the type and volume of work is always subject to change.","sub":[]}]},{"h":"COMMENCEMENT OF EMPLOYMENT","items":[{"t":"Your employment begins on {{start}}. No previous employment counts as part of your period of continuous employment.","sub":[]}]},{"h":"PROBATIONARY PERIOD","items":[{"t":"You join us on an initial probationary period of three months. During this period your performance and general suitability will be assessed. If they are satisfactory, your employment will continue.","sub":[]},{"t":"If your performance is not up to the required standard, or you are considered generally unsuitable, we may take remedial action, which may include extending your probationary period, or we may terminate your employment at any time in accordance with clause 20.","sub":[]},{"t":"You will be informed in writing of the outcome of your probationary period. You should not consider your probationary period to have been passed until you have received that notification.","sub":[]},{"t":"We reserve the right not to apply our full contractual capability and disciplinary procedures during your probationary period.","sub":[]}]},{"h":"PLACE OF WORK","items":[{"t":"Your normal place of work is Bar Finch, 31 Cork Street, London W1S 3NQ. You will not be required to work outside the United Kingdom.","sub":[]}]},{"h":"WORKING HOURS","items":[{"t":"Your normal working hours are {{hours}} per week, worked over five days between Monday and Saturday. Your working days and shift times will be set by rota and may vary from week to week. Shifts will be scheduled between 7am and midnight.","sub":[]},{"t":"Rotas will normally be published at least seven days in advance.","sub":[]},{"t":"You will not be required to work on more than five days in any week. You may agree to work a sixth day, but you are not obliged to do so.","sub":[]},{"t":"So far as reasonably practicable, rotas will be planned so that a closing shift is not followed by an opening shift the next day. Where the interval between your shifts is less than 11 hours, you will receive an equivalent period of compensatory rest within a reasonable time.","sub":[]},{"t":"Your average working time, including additional hours, will not exceed 48 hours per week averaged over the applicable reference period unless you have signed a separate opt-out agreement. Signing an opt-out is voluntary and is not a condition of your employment.","sub":[]},{"t":"If your rota regularly requires you to work three hours or more between 11pm and 6am, you will be offered a free health assessment before starting that pattern and at regular intervals while it continues.","sub":[]},{"t":"These working hours and rest break provisions apply to employees aged 18 or over. If you are under 18, different limits apply and you will be issued with a separate statement of terms.","sub":[]}]},{"h":"REST BREAKS","items":[{"t":"On each working day on which you work more than six hours, you will receive a paid, uninterrupted rest break of at least 20 minutes. Your break will be scheduled by the manager on duty, will not be placed at the start or end of your shift, and may be spent away from your workstation.","sub":[]},{"t":"If your break is interrupted by the needs of service, it will be restarted, or a replacement break will be provided during the same shift.","sub":[]},{"t":"On shifts of eight hours or more you will receive a further paid break of 20 minutes, normally coinciding with the staff meal.","sub":[]}]},{"h":"REMUNERATION","items":[{"t":"Your wage is currently £{{rate}} per hour, paid monthly in arrears on the 23rd of each month by bank transfer, as detailed on your payslip.","sub":[]}]},{"h":"ADDITIONAL HOURS","items":[{"t":"You may be required to work additional hours where the needs of the business require it. Additional hours must be authorised in advance by your Manager. Where additional hours are authorised and reasonable notice is given, you are expected to work them.","sub":[]},{"t":"Additional hours will be paid at your basic hourly rate.","sub":[]}]},{"h":"DEDUCTIONS","items":[{"t":"We may deduct from your pay, or require you to repay, any sums you owe to the Company. These include any overpayment of wages or expenses, the cost of training repayable under clause 14, and payment for holiday taken in excess of your accrued entitlement under clause 11. You authorise these deductions for the purposes of the Employment Rights Act 1996.","sub":[]}]},{"h":"BENEFITS","items":[{"t":"There are no contractual benefits applicable to your employment. Please speak to your Manager to find out what non-contractual benefits are currently available.","sub":[]}]},{"h":"HOLIDAY ENTITLEMENT","items":[{"t":"The holiday year runs from 1 April to 31 March. Your paid holiday entitlement is 28 days per holiday year, inclusive of the usual public holidays in England and Wales.","sub":[]},{"t":"Because of the nature of the business, you may be required to work on a public holiday as rostered. No premium is payable for working a public holiday, and the day remains part of your 28 day entitlement, to be taken at another time.","sub":[]},{"t":"In your first and final years of employment your entitlement is calculated pro rata. Entitlement is also calculated pro rata for part-time employees.","sub":[]},{"t":"Holiday must be requested in advance through your Manager and is subject to approval. You should give notice of at least twice the length of the holiday requested. We may refuse a request, or may require you to take holiday on specified dates, including during any closure period or during your notice period, by giving you notice of at least twice the length of the period concerned.","sub":[]},{"t":"Holiday must be taken in the year in which it accrues. Untaken holiday is lost at the end of the holiday year, except where the law requires carry-over, for example following sickness absence or statutory family leave, in which case the statutory rules apply.","sub":[]},{"t":"On termination you will be paid in lieu of holiday accrued but not taken. If at your termination date you have taken more holiday than you have accrued, the excess will be deducted from your final pay in accordance with clause 9.","sub":[]}]},{"h":"HOLIDAY PAY","items":[{"t":"Where your pay does not vary, your holiday pay is your normal pay.","sub":[]},{"t":"Where your pay varies, a week’s holiday pay is your average weekly earnings over the previous 52 weeks in which wages were payable, ignoring any week in which no wages were payable and looking back no more than 104 weeks. If you have been employed for fewer than 52 complete weeks, the average is taken over the number of complete weeks you have worked.","sub":[]},{"t":"Holiday pay includes payments that form part of your normal remuneration, such as regular additional hours payments. It does not include amounts distributed through the tronc, which are not wages payable by the Company.","sub":[]}]},{"h":"OTHER PAID LEAVE","items":[{"t":"Subject to any qualifying criteria and notification requirements, you are entitled to the following types of paid leave in line with the statutory entitlements in force from time to time:","sub":["maternity, paternity, adoption, shared parental, and neonatal care leave; and","parental bereavement leave for qualifying parents."]},{"t":"Further details of these entitlements, and of unpaid statutory leave, are set out in the Employee Handbook.","sub":[]}]},{"h":"TRAINING","items":[{"t":"At the start of your employment you will receive training for your specific job. As your employment progresses, your skills may be extended to cover new job activities within the business. It is a condition of your employment that you participate in any training we consider necessary for you to reach the required standard.","sub":[]},{"t":"The cost of mandatory training will be borne by the Company.","sub":[]},{"t":"We encourage employees to undertake external training courses that may further their career with us. Financial assistance may be provided where your Manager believes the Company will benefit from your progression. Any assistance will be subject to a training agreement requiring you to repay the cost of the training to the Company on a sliding scale if your employment ends. Further details are available from your Manager.","sub":[]}]},{"h":"SICK PAY","items":[{"t":"There is no contractual sick pay scheme. You will be paid Statutory Sick Pay in accordance with the statutory scheme in force from time to time, provided you meet its conditions. The sickness absence procedure is set out in the Employee Handbook.","sub":[]}]},{"h":"PENSION","items":[{"t":"Where required, we operate a contributory pension scheme into which you will be auto-enrolled, subject to the conditions of the scheme. Further details are available separately.","sub":[]}]},{"h":"COLLECTIVE AGREEMENTS","items":[{"t":"No collective agreements directly affect your terms and conditions of employment.","sub":[]}]},{"h":"DISCIPLINARY AND CAPABILITY PROCEDURE","items":[{"t":"The Company’s disciplinary and capability rules, and the procedures that apply to capability and disciplinary issues, dismissals, and appeals, are set out in the Employee Handbook. They do not form part of your contract of employment.","sub":[]},{"t":"If you are dissatisfied with a capability or disciplinary decision, you should apply, either verbally or in writing, to your Manager within five working days of the decision.","sub":[]}]},{"h":"GRIEVANCE PROCEDURE","items":[{"t":"If you are aggrieved about any matter relating to your employment, you should raise the grievance with your Manager, either verbally or in writing. If you are dissatisfied with the outcome of the formal grievance procedure, you may appeal in writing to the Director.","sub":[]},{"t":"Further information is set out in the Employee Handbook. The grievance procedure does not form part of your contract of employment.","sub":[]}]},{"h":"NOTICE PERIODS","items":[{"t":"Notice to be given by you:","sub":["under one month’s service: none;","from one month’s service until successful completion of your probationary period: one week; and","after successful completion of your probationary period: one month."]},{"t":"Notice to be given by the Company:","sub":["under one month’s service: none;","from one month’s service until successful completion of your probationary period: one week;","after successful completion of your probationary period but with less than two years’ service: one month; and","with two years’ service or more: one week for each completed year of service, up to a maximum of 12 weeks."]}]},{"h":"PAY IN LIEU OF NOTICE","items":[{"t":"We reserve the contractual right to make a payment of basic pay in lieu of all or any part of the notice period set out above, whether notice is given by you or by the Company.","sub":[]}]},{"h":"CHANGES TO YOUR TERMS","items":[{"t":"We will notify you in writing of any change to these terms within one month of the change taking effect. Minor changes of detail may be made by way of general notice to employees; any other change will be made only after consultation with you.","sub":[]}]},{"h":"DECLARATION","items":[{"t":"I acknowledge receipt of this statement and confirm my agreement to the terms and conditions set out above and in the Employee Handbook.","sub":[]}]}]};
